r/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5} \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715249}] [{:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2} e^{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715250}] [{:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{5}}{5 \\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715251}] [{:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} + \\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715253}] [{:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2} \\left(- e^{3} + e^{8}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715255}] [{:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{2} e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715256}] [{:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{5}}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715258}] [{:answer/feedback "$\\frac52$ is the squared magnitude. Take its square root." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715371}] [{:answer/feedback "A magnitude is nonnegative. The negative component indicates a leftward direction." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715372}] [{:answer/feedback "$(-2)^2=4$, so the radicand is $4+16=20$, not $-4+16=12$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715375}] [{:answer/feedback "Line (1) correctly uses the sum of the squared components. Negative components must still be squared, not subtracted." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Line (1); the magnitude is $\\sqrt{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715376}] [{:answer/feedback "Correct: $|\\mathbf{b}|^2=\\frac94+\\frac14=\\frac52$, so $|\\mathbf{b}|=\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}2$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715377}] [{:answer/feedback "Line (2) squares both components correctly, including the negative sign and denominators. The first error occurs in line (3)." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Line (2); the magnitude is $\\sqrt{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715379}] [{:answer/feedback "Both component squares are positive. Subtracting them gives $\\frac94-\\frac14=2$, but the formula adds them." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715380}] [{:answer/feedback "Correct: line (3) improperly distributes the square root. Adding first gives $\\sqrt{\\frac84}=\\sqrt2$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Line (3); the magnitude is $\\sqrt{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715381}] [{:answer/feedback "Line (3) is the first error, but $2$ is the squared magnitude. The magnitude is $\\sqrt2$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Line (3); the magnitude is $2$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715382}] [{:answer/feedback "A square root does not distribute over a sum. Here $\\sqrt{\\frac34+\\frac54}=\\sqrt2$, not $\\frac{\\sqrt3+\\sqrt5}{2}$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No line is incorrect; the magnitude is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{5}}{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715384}] [{:answer/feedback "$2$ is the sum of the absolute components, not their Euclidean length." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715385}] [{:answer/feedback "Squaring a fraction also squares its denominator: $\\left(\\frac32\\right)^2=\\frac94$, not $\\frac92$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715388}] [{:answer/feedback "$20$ is the sum of the squares, which is the squared magnitude. Take its square root." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715389}] [{:answer/feedback "Adding the leg lengths gives $2+4=6$, not the hypotenus